  "rationale": [
    "Operative S is the declared scientific priority at G-selected checkpoints.",
    "Name and residue-atom pair improves operative S over the default full-source configuration in all four V10f seeds.",
    "Low initial activity produces strong attenuation and surface closures without consistent S/G improvement.",
    "Higher penalties and progressive schedules do not establish useful chemical source elimination.",
    "Keep historical curvature channels and learned gates at the reference policy instead of promoting unconfirmed sparsity.",
    "Retain a contemporary historical-input control for independent confirmation."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The four seeds were used to compare 20 policies; this is a development decision.",
    "Name-pair versus trained forced-closed control has mixed signs and a small uncertain mean S advantage.",
    "Name-pair does not improve raw S versus the default full-source configuration.",
    "Low deterministic gates are not biological importance and can be compensated by later weights.",
    "New chemical sources remain available in the reusable system for other tasks; their global inventories are not deleted."
  ],
